<title>FINLAND: SOCCER-FINLAND BEAT AZERBAIJAN 3-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-FINLAND BEAT AZERBAIJAN 3-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI, Finland 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland beat</p>
<p>Azerbaijan 3-0 (halftime 0-0) in their World Cup European group</p>
<p>three qualifier on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Jari Vanhala 59, Jari Litmanen 64, Antti Sumiala 81</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,417</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Finland - 1-Antti Niemi; 2-Kari Rissanen, 3-Sami Hyypia,</p>
<p>4-Jussi Nuorela, 5-Jukka Koskinen, 6-Sami Mahlio, 7-Jari</p>
<p>Vanhala, 8-Mika Nurmela (15-Simo Valakari 45), 9-Antti Sumiala,</p>
<p>10-Jari Litmanen (18-Kai Nyyssonen 83), 11-Jonatan Johansson</p>
<p>(14-Joonas Kolkka 61)</p>
<p>Azerbaijan - 1-Alexandr Jidkov; 2-Faik Jabbarov, 3-Deni</p>
<p>Gaissounov, 4-Tarlan Akhmedov (17-Bakhtiiar Moussaev 65),</p>
<p>5-Viatcheslav Lytchkin, 6-Rassim Abouchov, 7-Ionis Gousseinov,</p>
<p>8-Emine Agaev (14-Mirbaguir Issaev 89), 9-Roufat Kouliev,</p>
<p>10-Gourban Gourbanov, 11-Veli Kassoumov (18-Zaour Tagui-zade 61)</p>
<p>Referee: Alain Hamer (Luxembourg)</p>
</text>
